_score_int_coverage":23.7,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":2.706035832318664,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":28.8,"_gate_accruals":-0.032894155097709786,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":42.5,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.09310261300759202,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":87.7,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.021584971180266366,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":73.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":0.033614146783034315,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":16.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.19254415684810436,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":67.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.14771897859557698,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":65.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.2689539253833715,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.04065051801427699,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":23.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.01484642278442938,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":32.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.0013031785833279574,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":25.7,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.019384993849938498,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":19.4,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.023748319306594518,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":37.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.013295158815247343,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":66.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.005172413793103448,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.00046,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Norfolk Southern Corporation, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the rail transportation of raw materials, intermediate products, and finished goods in the United States. The company transports agriculture, forest, and consumer products comprising soybeans, wheat, corn, fertilizers, livestock and poultry feed, food products, food oils, flour, sweeteners, ethanol, lumber and wood products, pulp board and paper products, wood fibers, wood pulp, beverages, and canned goods; chemicals, including sulfur and related chemicals, petroleum products comprising crude oil, chlorine and bleaching compounds, plastics, rubber, industrial chemicals, chemical wastes, sand, and natural gas liquids; metals and construction materials, such as steel, aluminum products, machinery, scrap metals, cement, aggregates, minerals, clay, transportation equipment, and military-related products; and automotive, including finished motor vehicles and automotive parts, as well as coal. It also transports overseas freight through various Atlantic and Gulf Coast ports; and operates an intermodal network. Norfolk Southern Corporation was incorporated in 1980 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark R. George | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $4.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $631K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $112K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Norfolk Southern Corporation is a large-cap industrials business with a $73.6B market cap on $12.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $2.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.05314720493810911},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 27% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","43 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Norfolk Southern/Union Pacific deal spread widens amid report on UNP CEO's remarks","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4672619-norfolk-southernunion-pacific-deal-spread-widens-amid-report-on-unp-ceos-remarks","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794605819.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Billionaire Investor Dan Loeb Bought Back Into Union Pacific and Norfolk Southern In Q2 \u2014 Here's Where the $85 Billion Rail Merger Stands","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/11/63231581/dan-loeb-third-point-rebuys-union-pacific-norfolk-southern-stakes","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566528.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","m_and_a"]},{"title":"Schneider National (SNDR) Could Be 19% Undervalued After Earnings Beat And Norfolk Southern Deal","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nyse-sndr/schneider-national/news/schneider-national-sndr-could-be-19-undervalued-after-earnin","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794486851.37,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.681,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Canadian Pacific Kansas City (TSX:CP) Has Drawn Fresh Attention, But What Is Behind It?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/ca/transportation/tsx-cp/canadian-pacific-kansas-city-shares/news/canadian-pacific-kansas-city-tsxcp-has-drawn-fresh-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794533044.784,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"North Charleston receives grant to help fund Hazard Materials Program for NCFD","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.